<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss version="2.0"><channel><title>HaulTimes</title><link>https://haultimes.com/</link><description>Freight and trucking news for the US and Canada</description><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:41:26 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Hours of Service (HOS) of Drivers; American Pyrotechnics Association (APA); Request To Include an Additional Member Company to Current APA HOS Exemptions</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/hours-of-service-hos-of-drivers-american-pyrotechnics-association-apa-9a344ffa94/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/hours-of-service-hos-of-drivers-american-pyrotechnics-association-apa-9a344ffa94/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Federal Register (FMCSA)</description></item><item><title>At least 14 charged in alleged $22.5 million California train cargo theft scheme</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/at-least-14-charged-in-alleged-22-5-million-california-train-cargo-the-c02dac559f/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/at-least-14-charged-in-alleged-22-5-million-california-train-cargo-the-c02dac559f/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:12:55 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Federal prosecutors said at least 14 people have been charged over an alleged scheme that stole cargo worth $22.5 million from freight trains in Southern California. Prosecutors say the crew hit at least 36 freight trains between February 2024 and August 2026, cutting air hoses to force them to stop. Prosecutors identified Nathan Daniel Angel, 21, of East Los Angeles, as the alleged leader, operating with his father and two uncles. Officials said a Los Angeles-based sneaker resale business, which was not an authorized Nike reseller, bought stolen sneakers and generated more than $1 million for the crew. The defendants are presumed innocent, and the maximum penalties include five years for conspiracy and 10 years for each theft count.</description></item><item><title>Hydrogen-powered truck completes 1,046-km freight haul from Vancouver to Calgary</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/hydrogen-powered-truck-completes-1-046-km-freight-haul-from-vancouver-1056c5e2db/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/hydrogen-powered-truck-completes-1-046-km-freight-haul-from-vancouver-1056c5e2db/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:41:19 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>Laredo Border Hours, Reefer Risks, Flexport AI: Week in Logistics</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/laredo-border-hours-reefer-risks-flexport-ai-week-in-logistics-37adab6927/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/laredo-border-hours-reefer-risks-flexport-ai-week-in-logistics-37adab6927/</guid><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:23:30 +0000</pubDate><category>Cross-Border</category><description>U.S. Customs and Border Protection and Mexico&#x27;s National Customs Agency, known as ANAM, extended a Saturday commercial truck processing pilot at Laredo&#x27;s World Trade Bridge, with the window now running until 7 p.m. The roundup says the extension adds three hours and lifts Saturday crossings by 400 to 500 trucks, while easing bottlenecks on Sunday and Monday. It also notes that cross-border volumes have reached record highs.</description></item><item><title>Truck drivers stranded in snow along interstate in California mountains</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/truck-drivers-stranded-in-snow-along-interstate-in-california-mountain-8fab767786/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/truck-drivers-stranded-in-snow-along-interstate-in-california-mountain-8fab767786/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:56:32 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Yahoo</description></item><item><title>&#x27;Fraudulent&#x27; Forza ELD back on FMCSA registry of approved devices</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/fraudulent-forza-eld-back-on-fmcsa-registry-of-approved-devices-59b262d7bf/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/fraudulent-forza-eld-back-on-fmcsa-registry-of-approved-devices-59b262d7bf/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:13:42 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>www.overdriveonline.com</description></item><item><title>DOL sticks with independent contractor proposal, trucking applauds</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/dol-sticks-with-independent-contractor-proposal-trucking-applauds-1e6f3e0b31/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/dol-sticks-with-independent-contractor-proposal-trucking-applauds-1e6f3e0b31/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:47:24 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>TxDOT Has A Simple Warning For Truckers After Lubbock&#x27;s I-27 Bridge Accident</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/txdot-has-a-simple-warning-for-truckers-after-lubbock-s-i-27-bridge-ac-5af516eddd/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/txdot-has-a-simple-warning-for-truckers-after-lubbock-s-i-27-bridge-ac-5af516eddd/</guid><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 22:22:17 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The Department of Transportation (TxDOT) has spoken out about truck drivers striking overpasses in Texas. The column recalls an October semi crash into the I-27 overpass in Lubbock, where the driver misjudged the height, and cites a Houston bridge that has been hit 16 times since January 2025. TxDOT also identified 61 instances of unreported bridge damage so far in 2026. The writer lists improperly measured vehicle height, misunderstood clearance postings and ignored warning signs as common causes, and notes that oversized trucks need permits because some roads and bridges are not designed for them. The writer advises drivers to know their vehicle&#